# `yo fix <path> --migrate unsized` lists a `downcast` of an OWNED Dyn (its
# owning form is `Result(Box(V), Box(Dyn(...)))`), never one through a
# reference: `downcast(&b.*, V)` and `downcast(e, V)` with `e : &Dyn(...)` or
# `e : &Box(Dyn(...))` are views already, a `ref` target included (it keeps
# the retained `Option(V)`). The file is in the v0.2.78 spelling: the run
# rewrites and lists nothing, and the file still type-checks.
fix . --migrate unsized
check main.yo
